          <div class="case-body">
          <div class="prose">
            <p>I work from Lagos, mostly for companies based elsewhere, so this question is hard to ignore. I first asked it on stage at The Builders Summit. Now I’m turning it into open research for builders and investors, starting with public survey data and moving on to interviews and a yearly report.</p>
            <p>The early data is small, so treat it as a direction, not a market size. In Stack Overflow’s 2024 survey, 30.2% of African developers have a say in buying tools, compared with 21.7% globally. They also use AI assistants to evaluate tools far more often, which makes showing up in AI answers more important here. Most lean on open source and free tiers, and paying in dollars is still a real barrier.</p>
